<section aria-labelledby="kubernetes-ai-tasks">
  <h2 id="kubernetes-ai-tasks">What your agent can do</h2>
  <div class="mt-5 space-y-6">
    <div>
      <h3>Investigate unhealthy pods and container restarts</h3>
      <p>
        List <a href="#action-kubernetes.pods_list">pods</a>, check <a href="#action-kubernetes.events_warnings">warning events</a>, and read the
        container's <a href="#action-kubernetes.pod_previous_logs">previous logs</a>.
        Check the container state too: a pod can show Running while a container is in CrashLoopBackOff.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Check deployment progress and rollout history</h3>
      <p>
        Check <a href="#action-kubernetes.rollout_status">rollout status</a> for progress
        and <a href="#action-kubernetes.rollout_history">rollout history</a> for earlier
        revisions. Select the namespace, workload, and cluster context you want to investigate.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Request a rolling restart or rollback</h3>
      <p>
        <a href="#action-kubernetes.rollout_restart">Rolling restarts</a>
        and <a href="#action-kubernetes.rollout_undo">rollbacks</a>
        are high risk; a rollback starts a new rollout using a previous revision.
        Check the rollout and application health afterwards.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
